  "why": "The statement asks whether the assembly maps are isomorphisms for all groups, so every class-level theorem (hyperbolic, CAT(0), mapping class groups, colorable/decomposable HHGs, affine Artin B~n) is a case, never whole. DMS is an unreviewed but credible case by established authors; the Sisto survey is a coauthor's restatement, not digestion. The B~n corrigendum and Li–Roushon remark are journal-published cases kept as doubtful given the conceded earlier error and the unreconciled wording; whichever form (FICwF or plain FJC) the corrigendum delivers, it is a case for one family. The original 2018 claim is knocked down by the identified, conceded error in Proposition 4.1. Localising-invariant results: BKW still covers K-theory for its group classes, so case; Reis only removes an invariant-side hypothesis, so variant. Totally disconnected/Hecke-algebra work is an analogue (variant). Surveys, the book, the EZ-structure and the Whitehead-group paper settle nothing (none). No AI system is credited anywhere.",
